    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-16-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "16 Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001#sch-1-sec-16-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "(8) For the purposes of the definitions of prescribed offender and\nserious offender, a person is under sentence in relation to a\nprescribed offence or a serious offence if the person:\n(a) is serving a sentence in a prison (including a gaol, lock-up or\nother place of detention); or\n(b) is serving a sentence of a kind, or subject to an order of a\nkind, provided for in subsection 20AB(1) as a sentence or\norder that may be passed or made by a court, under that\nsection, in respect of a person convicted of a federal offence;\nor\n(c) is released under a parole order made under subsection\n19AL(1) or (2); or\n(d) is released on a licence granted under section 19AP; or\n(e) being a child or young person, is serving a sentence of a kind,\nor subject to an order of a kind, provided for in subsection\n20C(1) as a sentence or order that, under that section, may be\nimposed on the child or young person who in a State or\nTerritory is convicted of an offence against the law of the\nCommonwealth; or\n(f) is subject to an order made under Division 9 of Part 1B; or\n(g) is convicted and conditionally released as provided for in\nsubsection 20(1), either:\n(i) in the case of paragraph 20(1)(a)—without sentence\nbeing passed; or\n(ii) in the case of paragraph 20(1)(b)—after sentence has\nbeen passed.",
      "skos:definition": "(8) For the purposes of the definitions of prescribed offender and\nserious offender, a person is under sentence in relation to a\nprescribed offence or a serious offence if the person:\n(a) is serving a sentence in a prison (including a gaol, lock-up or\nother place of detention); or\n(b) is serving a sentence of a kind, or subject to an order of a\nkind, provided for in subsection 20AB(1) as a sentence or\norder that may be passed or made by a court, under that\nsection, in respect of a person convicted of a federal offence;\nor\n(c) is released under a parole order made under subsection\n19AL(1) or (2); or\n(d) is released on a licence granted under section 19AP; or\n(e) being a child or young person, is serving a sentence of a kind,\nor subject to an order of a kind, provided for in subsection\n20C(1) as a sentence or order that, under that section, may be\nimposed on the child or young person who in a State or\nTerritory is convicted of an offence against the law of the\nCommonwealth; or\n(f) is subject to an order made under Division 9 of Part 1B; or\n(g) is convicted and conditionally released as provided for in\nsubsection 20(1), either:\n(i) in the case of paragraph 20(1)(a)—without sentence\nbeing passed; or\n(ii) in the case of paragraph 20(1)(b)—after sentence has\nbeen passed.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-16-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-16-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-16-2-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-16-2-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-16-2-logic-alleninterval-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-16-2-logic-ltl-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3797e1e25ee9fe8fd21ea0a410aea61e42c6673994b23895b0ec1a6fc29c6e19",
      "skos:note": "A person is under sentence in relation to a prescribed offence or serious offence if they meet certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001#sch-1-sec-16-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "16 Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "(8) For the purposes of the definitions of prescribed offender and\nserious offender, a person is under sentence in relation to a\nprescribed offence or a serious offence if the person:\n(a) is serving a sentence in a prison (including a gaol, lock-up or\nother place of detention); or\n(b) is serving a sentence of a kind, or subject to an order of a\nkind, provided for in subsection 20AB(1) as a sentence or\norder that may be passed or made by a court, under that\nsection, in respect of a person convicted of a federal offence;\nor\n(c) is released under a parole order made under subsection\n19AL(1) or (2); or\n(d) is released on a licence granted under section 19AP; or\n(e) being a child or young person, is serving a sentence of a kind,\nor subject to an order of a kind, provided for in subsection\n20C(1) as a sentence or order that, under that section, may be\nimposed on the child or young person who in a State or\nTerritory is convicted of an offence against the law of the\nCommonwealth; or\n(f) is subject to an order made under Division 9 of Part 1B; or\n(g) is convicted and conditionally released as provided for in\nsubsection 20(1), either:\n(i) in the case of paragraph 20(1)(a)—without sentence\nbeing passed; or\n(ii) in the case of paragraph 20(1)(b)—after sentence has\nbeen passed."
    },
