      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n(6) The suspect or his or her representative:\n(a) may call or cross-examine the applicant for the order; and\n(b) may, with the leave of the magistrate, call or cross-examine\nany other witnesses; and\n(c) may address the magistrate.\n(6A) A magistrate must not give leave under paragraph (6)(b) unless the\nmagistrate is of the opinion that there are substantial reasons why,\nin the interests of justice, the witness should be called or\ncross-examined.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n(6) The suspect or his or her representative:\n(a) may call or cross-examine the applicant for the order; and\n(b) may, with the leave of the magistrate, call or cross-examine\nany other witnesses; and\n(c) may address the magistrate.\n(6A) A magistrate must not give leave under paragraph (6)(b) unless the\nmagistrate is of the opinion that there are substantial reasons why,\nin the interests of justice, the witness should be called or\ncross-examined.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-45-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-45-ss-6a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fc61fc4a50e655d12b70c909f99174b3a8932dca19bfcf9d8128e3cad72db45b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001#sch-1-sec-45",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45 Subsection 23WX(6)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n(6) The suspect or his or her representative:\n(a) may call or cross-examine the applicant for the order; and\n(b) may, with the leave of the magistrate, call or cross-examine\nany other witnesses; and\n(c) may address the magistrate.\n(6A) A magistrate must not give leave under paragraph (6)(b) unless the\nmagistrate is of the opinion that there are substantial reasons why,\nin the interests of justice, the witness should be called or\ncross-examined."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-45-ss-6",
