      "skos:note": "Authorisation required for forensic procedures on suspects Offender must be allowed to communicate with legal practitioner in private unless constable suspects reasonable grounds for evidence destruction."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001#sch-1-sec-22-2-ss-2",
