    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-22-2-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "22(1) Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001#sch-1-sec-22-2-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An offender gives informed consent to a forensic procedure if the\noffender consents after a constable:\n(a) requests the offender to consent to the forensic procedure\nunder section 23XWH; and\n(b) informs the offender about the forensic procedure in\naccordance with section 23XWJ; and\n(c) gives the offender the opportunity to communicate, or\nattempt to communicate, with a legal practitioner of the\noffender’s choice.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An offender gives informed consent to a forensic procedure if the\noffender consents after a constable:\n(a) requests the offender to consent to the forensic procedure\nunder section 23XWH; and\n(b) informs the offender about the forensic procedure in\naccordance with section 23XWJ; and\n(c) gives the offender the opportunity to communicate, or\nattempt to communicate, with a legal practitioner of the\noffender’s choice.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-22-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-22-2-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-22-2-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
