    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-26-2-ss-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26(8) Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001#sch-1-sec-26-2-ss-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "(8) An order under this section takes effect immediately. However, the\nperson who conducts any analysis of forensic material obtained as\na result of carrying out the forensic procedure on an offender must\nnot disclose the results of the analysis:\n(a) until the expiration of any appeal period or after the final\ndetermination of any appeal in relation to the offence\nconcerned, whichever is the later; or\n(b) if the conviction is quashed.\n23XWP  Carrying out forensic procedure following conviction",
      "skos:definition": "(8) An order under this section takes effect immediately. However, the\nperson who conducts any analysis of forensic material obtained as\na result of carrying out the forensic procedure on an offender must\nnot disclose the results of the analysis:\n(a) until the expiration of any appeal period or after the final\ndetermination of any appeal in relation to the offence\nconcerned, whichever is the later; or\n(b) if the conviction is quashed.\n23XWP  Carrying out forensic procedure following conviction",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-26-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
