    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-26-2-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26(1) Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001#sch-1-sec-26-2-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n(a) an offender is in prison or another place of detention; and\n(b) a judge or magistrate orders the offender to permit a forensic\nprocedure to be carried out under this Division;\nthe judge or magistrate may order that a constable and a Division 6\nperson be permitted to attend on the offender in the prison or place\nof detention to allow the forensic procedure to be carried out.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n(a) an offender is in prison or another place of detention; and\n(b) a judge or magistrate orders the offender to permit a forensic\nprocedure to be carried out under this Division;\nthe judge or magistrate may order that a constable and a Division 6\nperson be permitted to attend on the offender in the prison or place\nof detention to allow the forensic procedure to be carried out.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-26-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-26-2-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-26-2-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-26-2-ss-1-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c30106d3249317caf80f41bd79b4622dc9508e48d014a8b95eea02169745a514",
      "skos:note": "Order to permit forensic procedure in prison or detention place Serious offender must consent to intimate forensic procedure."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001#sch-1-sec-26-2-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26(1) Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n(a) an offender is in prison or another place of detention; and\n(b) a judge or magistrate orders the offender to permit a forensic\nprocedure to be carried out under this Division;\nthe judge or magistrate may order that a constable and a Division 6\nperson be permitted to attend on the offender in the prison or place\nof detention to allow the forensic procedure to be carried out."
    },
