      "cml:integrityHash": "362a05da63c94ba4c947d277b7f3d403fae6e6e43eda34d6830bf88d6a1e2bf9",
      "skos:note": "Offender must be provided with a copy of the record. Authorized applicant may apply for order to carry out non-intimate forensic procedure on child or incapable person who is a serious offender. Defines Division 6 person under Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001#sch-1-sec-26-2-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26(2) Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "(2) In subsection (1), Division 6 person means a person who, under\nDivision 6 as applied by section 23XWE, may carry out the\nforensic procedure."
    },
