      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If a judge or magistrate orders an offender who is not in a prison or\nanother place of detention to permit a forensic procedure to be\ncarried out, the judge or magistrate may order the offender to\nattend at a police station (or other place specified by the judge or\nmagistrate) within a period specified by the judge or magistrate to\nallow the forensic procedure to be carried out.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If a judge or magistrate orders an offender who is not in a prison or\nanother place of detention to permit a forensic procedure to be\ncarried out, the judge or magistrate may order the offender to\nattend at a police station (or other place specified by the judge or\nmagistrate) within a period specified by the judge or magistrate to\nallow the forensic procedure to be carried out.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-26-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-26-2-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
