    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-60",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "60 At the end of section 23YC",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001#sch-1-sec-60"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf, p.34",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n(2) If an order for the carrying out of a forensic procedure made under\nsection 23XWU or for the retention of forensic material under\nsection 23XWV specifies a period for which forensic material\nobtained as a result of the carrying out of the procedure may be\nretained, the forensic material is to be destroyed as soon as\npracticable after the end of the period.\n\nCarrying out of forensic procedures on volunteers and certain other persons  Division\n6B\nSection 23XWV\nCrimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001                   35",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\n(2) If an order for the carrying out of a forensic procedure made under\nsection 23XWU or for the retention of forensic material under\nsection 23XWV specifies a period for which forensic material\nobtained as a result of the carrying out of the procedure may be\nretained, the forensic material is to be destroyed as soon as\npracticable after the end of the period.\n\nCarrying out of forensic procedures on volunteers and certain other persons  Division\n6B\nSection 23XWV\nCrimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001                   35",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-60-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1321e9f616ebc8cfb06c602d46a63731214e0e809c3fb22c5cd26fbc68ac7cc1",
      "skos:note": "Forensic material must be destroyed after a specified period."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001#sch-1-sec-60",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "60 At the end of section 23YC",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 34,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n(2) If an order for the carrying out of a forensic procedure made under\nsection 23XWU or for the retention of forensic material under\nsection 23XWV specifies a period for which forensic material\nobtained as a result of the carrying out of the procedure may be\nretained, the forensic material is to be destroyed as soon as\npracticable after the end of the period.\n\nCarrying out of forensic procedures on volunteers and certain other persons  Division\n6B\nSection 23XWV\nCrimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001                   35"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-60-norm",
