    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-63",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "63 Subsection 23YD(4)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001#sch-1-sec-63"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf, p.35",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n(4) If a warrant for the apprehension of the suspect is issued during the\nperiod of 12 months after forensic material is taken, the forensic\nmaterial must be destroyed as soon as practicable after:\n(a) the warrant lapses; or\n(b) a period of 12 months elapses after the suspect is\napprehended.\n(5) A magistrate may, on application by a constable or the Director of\nPublic Prosecutions, extend for a period not exceeding 12 months\nthe period for which forensic material may be retained under this\nsection, if the magistrate is satisfied there are special reasons for\ndoing so.\n(6) A magistrate to whom an application is made under subsection (5)\nis not to extend the period unless:\n(a) the person from whom the forensic material was taken has\nbeen notified by the applicant for the extension that the\napplication has been made; and\n(b) the person or his or her legal representative or interview\nfriend (if any) has been given the opportunity to speak to or\nmake a submission to the magistrate concerning the\nextension.\n(7) An extension in relation to particular forensic material may be\ngiven on more than one occasion.\n(8) The magistrate is to ensure that the responsible person in relation\nto the DNA database system is notified of any extension given\nunder this section.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n(4) If a warrant for the apprehension of the suspect is issued during the\nperiod of 12 months after forensic material is taken, the forensic\nmaterial must be destroyed as soon as practicable after:\n(a) the warrant lapses; or\n(b) a period of 12 months elapses after the suspect is\napprehended.\n(5) A magistrate may, on application by a constable or the Director of\nPublic Prosecutions, extend for a period not exceeding 12 months\nthe period for which forensic material may be retained under this\nsection, if the magistrate is satisfied there are special reasons for\ndoing so.\n(6) A magistrate to whom an application is made under subsection (5)\nis not to extend the period unless:\n(a) the person from whom the forensic material was taken has\nbeen notified by the applicant for the extension that the\napplication has been made; and\n(b) the person or his or her legal representative or interview\nfriend (if any) has been given the opportunity to speak to or\nmake a submission to the magistrate concerning the\nextension.\n(7) An extension in relation to particular forensic material may be\ngiven on more than one occasion.\n(8) The magistrate is to ensure that the responsible person in relation\nto the DNA database system is notified of any extension given\nunder this section.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-63-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-63-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-63-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-63-ss-7"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-63-ss-8"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fc61fc4a50e655d12b70c909f99174b3a8932dca19bfcf9d8128e3cad72db45b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001#sch-1-sec-63",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "63 Subsection 23YD(4)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 35,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n(4) If a warrant for the apprehension of the suspect is issued during the\nperiod of 12 months after forensic material is taken, the forensic\nmaterial must be destroyed as soon as practicable after:\n(a) the warrant lapses; or\n(b) a period of 12 months elapses after the suspect is\napprehended.\n(5) A magistrate may, on application by a constable or the Director of\nPublic Prosecutions, extend for a period not exceeding 12 months\nthe period for which forensic material may be retained under this\nsection, if the magistrate is satisfied there are special reasons for\ndoing so.\n(6) A magistrate to whom an application is made under subsection (5)\nis not to extend the period unless:\n(a) the person from whom the forensic material was taken has\nbeen notified by the applicant for the extension that the\napplication has been made; and\n(b) the person or his or her legal representative or interview\nfriend (if any) has been given the opportunity to speak to or\nmake a submission to the magistrate concerning the\nextension.\n(7) An extension in relation to particular forensic material may be\ngiven on more than one occasion.\n(8) The magistrate is to ensure that the responsible person in relation\nto the DNA database system is notified of any extension given\nunder this section."
    },
