    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-36-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "36 Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001#sch-1-sec-36-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf, p.36",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n23YDAA  Destruction of forensic material taken from offender after\nconviction quashed\nThe constable who obtained an authority under section 23XWG,\n23XWK or 23XWO for the carrying out of a forensic procedure on\nan offender whose conviction is quashed after the making of the\norder must ensure that any forensic material obtained as a result of\nthe carrying out of the procedure is destroyed as soon as\npracticable after the conviction is quashed.\n23YDAB  Destruction of forensic material where related evidence is\ninadmissible\nIf a magistrate finds that evidence described in subsection 23XX(3)\nrelating to a forensic procedure is inadmissible under\nsection 23XX, the Commissioner must, as soon as practicable,\nensure that any forensic material taken from the person by that\nforensic procedure is destroyed.",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\n23YDAA  Destruction of forensic material taken from offender after\nconviction quashed\nThe constable who obtained an authority under section 23XWG,\n23XWK or 23XWO for the carrying out of a forensic procedure on\nan offender whose conviction is quashed after the making of the\norder must ensure that any forensic material obtained as a result of\nthe carrying out of the procedure is destroyed as soon as\npracticable after the conviction is quashed.\n23YDAB  Destruction of forensic material where related evidence is\ninadmissible\nIf a magistrate finds that evidence described in subsection 23XX(3)\nrelating to a forensic procedure is inadmissible under\nsection 23XX, the Commissioner must, as soon as practicable,\nensure that any forensic material taken from the person by that\nforensic procedure is destroyed.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-36-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-36-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-36-2-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "05a33c35b373d2bf1328f03ac569539f10a15ddf56a399e90d551d079e6f4aee",
      "skos:note": "Ensure destruction of forensic material after conviction quashed."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001#sch-1-sec-36-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "36 Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 36,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n23YDAA  Destruction of forensic material taken from offender after\nconviction quashed\nThe constable who obtained an authority under section 23XWG,\n23XWK or 23XWO for the carrying out of a forensic procedure on\nan offender whose conviction is quashed after the making of the\norder must ensure that any forensic material obtained as a result of\nthe carrying out of the procedure is destroyed as soon as\npracticable after the conviction is quashed.\n23YDAB  Destruction of forensic material where related evidence is\ninadmissible\nIf a magistrate finds that evidence described in subsection 23XX(3)\nrelating to a forensic procedure is inadmissible under\nsection 23XX, the Commissioner must, as soon as practicable,\nensure that any forensic material taken from the person by that\nforensic procedure is destroyed."
    },
