    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-23yp",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23YP Taking, retention and use of forensic material",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001#sch-1-sec-23yp"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf, p.46",
      "values:originalText": "Taking, retention and use authorised by laws of other jurisdictions\n(1) Nothing in this Part affects the taking, retention or use of forensic\nmaterial, or information obtained from forensic material, if the\ntaking, retention or use of the material is authorised by or under a\nlaw of a State or a Territory.\n(2) Forensic material, or information obtained from it, that was taken\nin accordance with a law of a State or a Territory may be retained\nor used for investigative, evidentiary or statistical purposes of the\nCommonwealth. The material or information may be retained or\nused even if its retention or use would, but for this subsection,\n\nDNA database system  Division 8A\nSection 23YQ\nCrimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001                   47\nconstitute a breach of, or failure to comply with, any provision of\nthis Part relating to the carrying out of forensic procedures.\nUse and retention of forensic material taken before commencement\nof subsection\n(3) Forensic material, or information obtained from it, that is taken in\naccordance with a law of a State or a Territory, as in force\nimmediately before the commencement of this subsection, may be\nretained or used for investigative, evidentiary or statistical\npurposes of the Commonwealth. The material or information may\nbe retained or used even if its retention or use would, but for this\nsubsection, constitute a breach of, or failure to comply with, any\nprovision of this Part relating to the carrying out of forensic\nprocedures.",
      "skos:definition": "Taking, retention and use authorised by laws of other jurisdictions\n(1) Nothing in this Part affects the taking, retention or use of forensic\nmaterial, or information obtained from forensic material, if the\ntaking, retention or use of the material is authorised by or under a\nlaw of a State or a Territory.\n(2) Forensic material, or information obtained from it, that was taken\nin accordance with a law of a State or a Territory may be retained\nor used for investigative, evidentiary or statistical purposes of the\nCommonwealth. The material or information may be retained or\nused even if its retention or use would, but for this subsection,\n\nDNA database system  Division 8A\nSection 23YQ\nCrimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001                   47\nconstitute a breach of, or failure to comply with, any provision of\nthis Part relating to the carrying out of forensic procedures.\nUse and retention of forensic material taken before commencement\nof subsection\n(3) Forensic material, or information obtained from it, that is taken in\naccordance with a law of a State or a Territory, as in force\nimmediately before the commencement of this subsection, may be\nretained or used for investigative, evidentiary or statistical\npurposes of the Commonwealth. The material or information may\nbe retained or used even if its retention or use would, but for this\nsubsection, constitute a breach of, or failure to comply with, any\nprovision of this Part relating to the carrying out of forensic\nprocedures.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
